      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right to be worried about such things however I think in this case it should be fine as the display is a limited environment and is not considered a trusted part of the boot flow execution.\n\nAn actor with such access would have already compromised control over the EC and therefore impacted a key part of the root of trust of the system therefore the small EEPROM space in the display panel would be inconsequential and certainly not a entry vector. Malformed EDID\u0027s can just as easily come though a open display connector as well so the content isn\u0027t considered trusted either.",
